<p>A missile struck inside the U.S. Embassy compound in Baghdad on Saturday. Iraqi security officials said it hit a helipad and sent smoke rising from the sprawling diplomatic complex. Other security sources said the embassy came under attack as explosions shook the Iraqi capital, though accounts differed on whether the weapon was a missile, projectile, or drone. The strike comes amid a tense regional standoff. The Hindu noted that the Baghdad embassy, one of the world’s largest U.S. diplomatic facilities, has been repeatedly targeted in the past by rockets and drones linked to Iran-aligned militias. RT described the attack as part of a broader escalation tied to the ongoing U.S.-Israeli campaign against Iran, now in its third week, along with rising threats to shipping through the Strait of Hormuz and possible new U.S. deployments to the region.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0sbQWVknW2DR0E5eZVZEJd0cgevRHYqbkFS8uK8lazsAtCjtcKoKGHtUdHyTAL21j10IvoZh4cdFtQurgmBSTHt0Puos1pDQOyt3_dqihaL3zeaqUuvHyH3X47nxXFIzQP4mtxrhdCXHpCrhC5xriALNbVGqJCf3_YjyQMfadq-0Bxs_2x_ts6D4hOQbfo3ILo5-ew' alt='U.S. Embassy compound in Baghdad after reports of a strike inside the grounds' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Damage remains unclear: Reuters, cited by Al-Monitor, said smoke rose from the embassy building after the strike, but security sources gave no further details about the extent of the damage.</li><li>A tense night in Baghdad: The Straits Times said reports of the embassy strike surfaced as explosions rocked Baghdad, placing the attack within a broader night of instability in the capital.</li><li>Pressure on an oil hub: RT said Trump tied continued restraint on Iran&#x27;s Kharg Island oil port to whether shipping through the Strait of Hormuz remains unobstructed.</li><li>U.S. forces on the move: RT also reported that the Pentagon was moving an amphibious assault-ready expeditionary unit, typically about 5,000 marines, into the region.</li></ul><blockquote>However, should Iran, or anyone else, do anything to interfere with the Free and Safe Passage of Ships through the Strait of Hormuz, I will immediately reconsider this decision - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iraqi security officials: Officials said the strike hit a helipad inside the U.S. Embassy compound and that smoke rose from the embassy building after the attack. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-embassy-in-baghdad-helipad-west-asia-conflict/article70742258.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Security sources in Baghdad: Sources offered differing accounts of the weapon, with one saying a drone hit the embassy and another saying it may have been a projectile. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/two-killed-in-strikes-on-iraq-capital-targeting-iran-backed-group-sources'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Tehran&#x27;s position: RT reported that Iran threatened to turn U.S.-linked oil infrastructure across the Middle East into a &quot;pile of ashes&quot; if its own facilities came under attack. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/634898-us-iran-israel-updates/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-embassy-in-baghdad-helipad-west-asia-conflict/article70742258.ece'>Missile strikes a helipad inside U.S. Embassy compound in Baghdad: Iraqi security officials</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/634898-us-iran-israel-updates/'>Missile hits US embassy in Iraq, as Trump exchanges oil threats with Iran (PHOTOS, VIDEOS)</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/two-killed-in-strikes-on-iraq-capital-targeting-iran-backed-group-sources'>Explosions rock Baghdad as security sources say US embassy attacked</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/us-embassy-iraqs-baghdad-hit-missiles-attack-security-sources-say'>US embassy in Iraq&#x27;s Baghdad hit in missiles attack, se